As envisioned, compounds 3 and 4 are isoreticular analogues of pek-MOF-1, named pek-MOF-2, constructed from the identical double $\bf k g m$ layers but at present connected together through elongated pillars, resulting in an increased spacing between the layers along the $\mathrm{{^c}}$ -axis as evident by the observed increase in the c parameter $(21.1\mathrm{\AA}$ versus $26.4\textup{\AA}$ in pek-MOF-1 and pek-MOF-2, respectively); (Figure S11, Supporting Information).
aea-MOF platform: The evident association of the pek-MOF structure with the kgm layer has prompted us to explore other 3-c ligands that might disturb the formation of the requisite kgm layer and prospectively, once again, promote the effect of the ligand geometrical attributes on the resulting topology.
Purposely, we opted to explore the carbazole-based ligands due to their associated contracted angle between the two carboxylate moieties, namely a $90^{\circ}$ angle as compared to $120^{\circ}$ in the isophthalate moiety.20 Accordingly, the 9-(4-carboxyphenyl)-9Hcarbazole-3,6-dicarboxylic acid (H3L3) tricarboxylate ligand, which has $90^{\circ}$ angle between carboxylate groups on the carbazole moiety, was designed and synthesized (Figure 1). Indeed, reactions of H3L3 with $\mathrm{Y(NO_{3})}_{3.6\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}}$ , in the presence of the cluster directing agent 2-FBA, resulted in the formation of colorless hexagonal crystals, characterized and formulated by SCXRD and elemental microanalysis studies as $|(\mathrm{DMA})_{1.3}$ $(\mathrm{Y}_{9}(\upmu_{3}{\mathrm{-OH}})_{12}(\upmu_{3}-$ $\mathrm{O)_{2}(Y_{1.2})(H_{2}O)_{9}(2-F B z o a t e)_{12})_{0.33}|[Y_{9}(Y_{0.28})(\mu_{3}-O H)_{12}]_{0.33}+\Delta_{0}(O H)_{2}}$ 2(μ3- $\mathrm{O)_{2}(H_{2}O)_{9}(Y_{9}(\mu_{3}-O H)_{12}(\mu_{3}-O)_{2}(H_{2}O)_{9})_{2}({\bf L}{\bf}{\bf}{\bf}{\bf}{3})_{12}].(\mathrm{solv})_{\bf x}}$ (5). $(\mathbf{L}3\mathbf{\Psi}=$ $\mathrm{C_{15}H_{7}O_{6}}$ , 2-FBzoate $={\mathrm{C}}_{7}{\mathrm{H}}_{4}{\mathrm{FO}}_{2}^{\cdot}$ ).
The SCXRD study discloses that compound 5 crystallizes in a primitive hexagonal space group $P6/m m m$ . Analysis of the resultant crystal structure of 5 reveals the formation of a novel 3- periodic highly-connected Y-MOF based solely on nonanuclear Y carboxylate-based clusters, formed in situ, and similar to the 12- c nonanuclear RE cluster observed in the pek-MOF. Specifically, the structure encloses three crystallographically independent nonanuclear clusters, each built by nine yttrium (Y) ions and capped by 12 carboxylate moieties, but only two of the nonanuclear clusters are copolymerized by the fully deprotonated tricarboxylate ligands (L3) to form a 3-periodic MOF hosting the third discrete nonanuclear cluster, capped by 12 carboxylate moieties from terminal 2-fluorobenzoate ligands, in its porous system.
From a topological analysis perspective, the two nonanuclear clusters, 12-connected MBBs, have the same d6R vertex figure as observed in the pek-MOF, but are topologically distinct and thus their assembly with the 3-c ligand reveals the discovery of a novel highly-connected Y-MOF with a trinodal (3,12,12)-c net and aea underlying topology, Y-aea-MOF-1  (Figure 1). Analogous to the pek net, the new trinodal aea net is a minimal edge transitive net, transitivity [3244], and is an appropriate target for MOF crystal chemistry.
The purity of compounds 5 was confirmed by similarities between the experimental and calculated powder X-ray diffraction (PXRD) patterns (Figures S5, Supporting Information).
The aea-MOF-1 structure encloses a rhombic-like cage with estimated diameters of $9.2\substack{-13.7\mathrm{~\AA~}}$ (height) and $14.8\mathrm{~\AA~}$ (width), taking vdW radius into consideration, having two separate apertures with relative dimensions of $5.2\times3.5\mathrm{~\AA~}$ and $10\times\hat{5}.4\mathrm{~\AA~}$ . In addition, the structure possesses three intersecting infinite square channels with an estimated diameter of $12.5\mathrm{\AA}$ (Figure S12, Supporting Information).
The corresponding solvent accessible free volume for 5 was estimated to be $55\%$ , by summing voxels more than $1.2\textup{\AA}$ away from the framework using PLATON software.17
Interestingly and similarly to the pek-MOF, the structure of aeaMOF-1 can be deconstructed into 2-periodic layers pillared by 12- c nonanuclear clusters. The layers are composed of one kind of nonanuclear clusters where each nonanuclear cluster is surrounded by three neighboring nonanuclear clusters, and linked in the plane, to afford their subsequent arrangement in a 2-periodic sheet reminiscent of a honeycomb (hcb) lattice. The resultant hcb layers are further intercalated by a periodic array of the second and distinct nonanuclear clusters arranged in a hexagonal layer manner where each nonanuclear cluster superimposes with the two adjacent hexagonal rings (Figure 3). Correspondingly, the aeaMOF structure can also be regarded as built from pillared layers. Specifically, when considering only the carbazole dicarboxylate part of the 3- c ligand (i.e. discounting the connectivity via the benzoate moieties), it is possible to isolate some bidimensional layers, where each nonanuclear cluster is quadruply connected to each of three neighboring others via four carbazole dicarboxylate moieties (Figure 3). Topological simplification of the resultant 2- periodic arrangement reveals the occurrence of an hcb layer, considered in this case as a quadruply cross-linked hcb. We envision the newly discovered (3,12,12)-c aea net and the quadruply cross-linked hcb layer as promising blueprints for the directed assembly of highly-connected and pillared MOFs using the SBL approach.
Gas sorption studies: In order to assess the porosity of the resultant pek- and aea-MOFs, and subsequently explore their potential for gas separations and gas storage, adsorption isotherms were collected using several probe molecules at various temperatures and pressures.
The Ar adsorption isotherm recorded at $87\mathrm{K}$ showed that 1 and 2 analogues of pek-MOF-1 exhibit fully reversible Type-I isotherm (Figures 4), indicative of a porous material with permanent microporosity. The apparent–BET surface area and associated total pore volume were estimated to be $1330\mathrm{m}^{2}\mathrm{g}^{-1}\mathrm{and}0.47\mathrm{cm}^{3}\mathrm{g}^{-1}$ for 1, and $1608\mathrm{m}^{2}\mathrm{g}^{-1}$ and $0.58\ \mathrm{cm}^{3}\mathrm{g}^{-1}$ for 2. The experimentally obtained total pore volumes are in excellent agreement with the associated theoretical values derived from SCXRD data, i.e. 0.47 $\mathrm{cm}^{3}\mathrm{g}^{-1}$ for 1 and $0.58~\mathrm{cm}^{3}\mathrm{g}^{-1}$ for 2. The pore size distribution (PSD) for 1 was assessed using the Ar adsorption data (Figure S15, Supporting Information) and revealed two type of pores with average sizes centered around $10\mathrm{\AA}$ (cage) and $\bar{16.8\AA}$ (channels), which are in good qualitative agreement with the theoretical values derived from the associated crystal structure (8 and $13.5\mathrm{\AA}$ , respectively). Akin porosity study based on Ar adsorption was performed on 5 (Figures 4) and presented an apparent BET surface area and a total pore volume of $1435~\mathrm{m}^{2}\mathrm{g}^{-1}$ and $0.49\ \mathrm{cm}^{3}\mathrm{g}^{-1}$ respectively. The PSD for 5 showed two distinct pores with diameters around 16Å (cage) and $11\mathrm{\AA}$ (channels) (Figure S16, Supporting Information), in good qualitative agreement with the theoretical values derived from the associated crystal structure (14, $12.5\mathrm{\AA}$ , respectively).
In the light of our findings regarding the permanent porosity of pek-MOFs and aea-MOF-1, from both the theoretical and experimental point of view, we directed our efforts to the evaluation of the potential use of pek-MOF-1 in a number of energy relevant applications, such as $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ storage, $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ capture and light hydrocarbon separation. Examination of excess and absolute $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ gravimetric $\left(\mathrm{cm}^{3}\left(\mathrm{STP}\right)\mathrm{g}^{-1}\right)$ ) and volumetric $\left(\mathrm{cm}^{3}\left(\mathrm{STP}\right)\mathrm{cm}^{-3}\right)$ uptakes at intermediate and high pressures (Figure 5) showed that compound 2 and 1 methane uptakes are 150, 175 $\mathrm{RE}=\mathrm{Y},$ ) and 140, 166 $\mathrm{RE}=\mathrm{Tb}$ ) $\mathrm{cm}^{3}$ (STP) $\mathrm{cm}^{-3}$ at 35 and 50 bar, respectively. The resulting $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ working storage capacities, assuming 35 bar (following the US Department of Energy standard)21 or 50 bar as the highest adsorption pressure limit and 5 bar as the lowest desorption pressure limit, are estimated to be 110, 135 and 97, $123\mathrm{cm}^{3}$ (STP) $\mathrm{cm}^{-3}$ , 2 and 1, respectively. It is worth noting that for the volumetric uptakes calculation, the density of pek-MOFs was assumed to be constant and equivalent to the theoretical density derived from the fully evacuated associated crystal structure (1.02 and $1.25~\mathrm{g}{\cdot}\mathrm{cm}^{-3}$ for the 2 and 1 analogues, respectively). A comparative tabulated data for the best performing $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ storage MOFs is reported in Table S1 (Table S1, Supporting Information)
Figure 6a, displaying the volumetric $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ uptake for pek-MOFs in comparison with various relevant MOFs, shows that 2 and 1 exhibit a relatively very high volumetric $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ uptake at 25 bar and $298\mathrm{~K~}$ . Specifically, the 2 exhibits $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ uptake of $288~\mathrm{cm}^{3}$ (STP) $\mathrm{cm}^{-3}$ that is slightly higher than MOF-177 $(273\ \mathrm{cm}^{3}\left(\mathrm{STP}\right)\mathrm{cm}^{-3}),^{\cdot}$ 22
HKUST-1 $276~\mathrm{cm}^{3}$ (STP) $\mathrm{cm}^{-3}$ ), $^{23}\mathrm{\:Mg-MOF-74}$ $285~\mathrm{cm}^{3}$ (STP) $\mathrm{cm}^{-3}$ ),24 MOF-5 $225\ \mathrm{cm}^{3}$ (STP) $\mathrm{cm}^{-3}$ ),22 gea-MOF-1 $224\ \mathrm{cm}^{3}$ $\mathrm{(STP)}\ \mathrm{cm}^{-3}\mathrm{\rangle}$ ,5c MOF-210 $(127~\mathrm{cm}^{3}\:(\mathrm{STP})\:\mathrm{cm}^{-3}.$ ),22 MOF-200 (112 $\mathrm{cm}^{3}\:\:(\mathrm{STP})\:\:\mathrm{cm}^{-3})^{22}$ but lower than rht-MOF-amide $(\mathrm{N},\mathrm{N},\mathrm{N}^{\prime\prime}.$ - tris(isophthalyl)-1,3,5-benzenetricarboxamide, TPBTM) $325~\mathrm{cm}^{3}$ $(\mathrm{STP})\mathrm{cm}^{-3})^{25}$ and rht-MOF-9 $(343\mathrm{cm}^{3}(\mathrm{STP})\mathrm{cm}^{-3}).^{2}$ 6 1 was found to uptake a relatively reduced $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ $(261\ \mathrm{cm}^{3}\ (\mathrm{STP})\ \mathrm{cm}^{-3})$ . These outstanding $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ volumetric uptakes for the RE-pek-MOF-1 at 25 bar could be explained by the combination of high porosity and high localized charge density, induced by the presence of both the nonanuclear and hexanuclear clusters, and the pending 2- fluorobenzoate moieties in the cavities. This combined effect led to moderate $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ -framework interactions in the range of 38-32 $\mathrm{kJ.mol^{-1}}$ at low $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ loading (Figures S17 and S18, Supporting Information) but a relatively high uptakes/density of $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ in the framework of RE-pek-MOF-1.
With the particular open structure of RE-pek-MOF-1 and its associated low uptakes of $\mathrm{H}_{2}$ , and $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ at low pressures, indicative of reasonably weak sorbate-framework interactions/affinity, (Figure S19 and S20, Supporting Information) as compared to larger and highly polarizable probe molecules (Figure 7a), we found it compelling to explore the potential of 1 for the removal of hydrocarbons from relevant gas streams. Condensable gases such as $\mathrm{C}_{}\mathrm{3H}_{8}$ and $\scriptstyle n-C_{4}\mathrm{H}_{10}$ present in gas streams containing valuable commodities such as $\mathrm{H}_{2}$ and $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ are undesirable and need to be subsequently removed. Accordingly, in addition to $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ , single gas adsorption properties of $C_{2}\mathrm{H}_{6}$ , $\mathrm{C}_{3}\mathrm{H}_{8}$ and $\scriptstyle n-C_{4}\mathrm{H}_{10}$ were investigated at $298\mathrm{~K~}$ and confronted with the corresponding properties of $\mathrm{H}_{2}$ and CH4.
It is worth noting that our group recently reported on the great potential of MOFs for light hydrocarbon separation.5c, 27 Interestingly, the $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ , $C_{2}\mathrm{H}_{6}$ , $\mathrm{{C_{3}H_{8}}}$ and $\scriptstyle n-C_{4}\mathrm{H}_{10}$ adsorption isotherms were reasonably much steeper at low pressures than those for $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ and $\mathrm{H}_{2}$ , indicative of the preferential adsorption affinity for 1, particularly to $C_{3}\mathrm{H}_{8}$ and $\scriptstyle n-C_{4}\mathrm{H}_{10}$ vs. $\mathrm{H}_{2}$ and $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ . Examination of single gas adsorption data using Ideal Adsorption Solution Theory (IAST) confirmed that 1 exhibits high adsorption selectivity for various gas pair systems such as $\mathrm{C_{3}H_{8}/C H_{4}}$ and $n\mathrm{.}$ - $\mathrm{C_{4H_{10}/C H_{4}}}$ (Figure 7b). Due to the insignificant uptakes of $\mathrm{H}_{2}$ on 1 at $298\mathrm{~K~}$ , adequate prediction of $\mathrm{C}_{3}\mathrm{H}_{8}/\mathrm{H}_{2}$ , $\boldsymbol{n}{-}\mathbf{C}_{4}\mathrm{H}_{10}{/}\mathbf{C}\mathrm{H}_{2}$ and $\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{H}_{2}$ was not possible. Nevertheless, the less selective adsorption of $\mathrm{H}_{2}$ when compared to $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ presents the pek-MOFs as an excellent candidate for $\mathrm{H}_{2}$ separation/purification. Therefore, pek-MOFs can be employed as separation agents for production of these valuable commodities $\mathrm{\tilde{H}}_{2}$ and $\mathrm{CH}_{4}^{\cdot}$ ) from many gas streams relevant to natural gas, biogas and petrochemical industry.
## CONCLUSIONS
We reported here the discovery of two fascinating and highlyconnected nets having novel pek and aea topologies via a systematic exploration on the use of RE metal salts in combination with relatively less symmetrical 3-c tricarboxylate ligands instead of the parent symmetrical tricarboxylate ligand, $\mathrm{\DeltaH_{3}B T B}$ . The implemented relatively lower symmetry of the 3-c tricarboxylate ligand was presumably responsible in driving the simultaneous occurrence of nonanuclear [RE9 $\left(\upmu_{3}{\mathrm{-OH}}\right)_{12}(\upmu_{3}{\mathrm{-O}})_{2}(\mathrm{O}2\mathrm{C}-\right)_{12}]$ and hexanuclear $\mathrm{\small{[RE_{6}(O H)_{8}(O_{2}C_{-})_{8}]}}$ carboxylate-based clusters to form novel 3-periodic pek-MOFs. Subsequent use of another 3-c tricarboxylate ligand with further contracted angles between the carboxylates (from $120^{\circ}$ to $90^{\circ}$ ) led to the formation of a second highly-connected net, (3,12,12)-c with an unprecedented aea topology. Notably, pek-MOF and aea-MOF are so far the first examples of RE-MOFs containing 12-c d6R SBUs which are exceptionally promising building units for the practice of reticular chemistry and subsequently the design of new highly-connected MOFs. The pek-MOF and aea-MOF are also the first examples of pillar-based MOFs where pillars manifest a relatively high connectivity (12-c), a unique feature that offer potential for the practice of the SBL approach for the design and directed assembly of highly-connected MOFs. The exceptional structural features of pek-MOFs were directly concomitant with their excellent $\mathrm{CH}_{4},$ , $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ storage properties as well as their promising gas separation potential for gas pair systems such as $\mathrm{C_{3}H_{8}/C H_{4}}$ , $\boldsymbol{n}{-}\mathrm{C}_{4}\mathrm{H}_{10}{/}\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ relevant to natural gas upgrading. There is no doubt that the ongoing design and development of finely tailored isoreticular pek and aea MOFs using the SBL approach will lead to enhanced gas storage and gas/vapor separation properties. Accordingly, work is in progress to construct isoreticular MOFs based on pek and aea topologies from various functional ligands.
