Materials and methods. Details on the synthesis of organic ligands used in this study, biphenyl-3,4̍,5-tricarboxylic acid $\mathbf{(H_{3}L1)}$ , 5-(4-carboxybenzyloxy)isophthalic acid $\mathbf{(H_{3}L2)}$ and 9-(4- carboxyphenyl)-9H-carbazole-3,6-dicarboxylic acid (H3L3) are provided in the Supporting information.
Single-crystal X-ray diffraction data were collected using a Bruker-AXS SMART-APEX2 CCD diffractometer $\mathrm{{Cu}\ K a}$ , $\lambda=$ $1.54178\mathrm{\AA}$ ). Fourier-transform infrared (FT-IR) spectra $(4000-600$ $\mathrm{cm}^{-1}.$ were collected in the solid state on a Nicolet 700 FT-IR spectrometer. The peak intensities are described in each of the spectra as very strong (vs), strong (s), medium (m), weak (w), broad (br) and shoulder (sh). Elemental analysis was performed with a Thermo Scientific Flash 2000 instrument. Powder X-ray diffraction (PXRD) measurements were performed on a PANalytical X’Pert PRO MPD $\mathrm{\DeltaX}$ -ray diffractometer at $45\mathrm{kV}$ , 40 mA for $\mathrm{{Cu}\ K a}$ $(\lambda~=~1.5418~\mathrm{~\AA~}$ ) equipped with a variabletemperature stage, with a scan speed of $20/\mathrm{min}$ . The sample was held at the designated temperatures for at least $10~\mathrm{min}$ between each scan. High resolution dynamic thermal gravimetric analysis (TGA) were performed under a continuous ${\bf N}_{2}$ flow and recorded on a TA Instruments hi-res TGAQ500 thermal gravimetric analyzer. Low pressure gas sorption measurements were performed on a fully automated Autosorb-iQ gas sorption analyzer (Quantachrome Instruments) and a fully automated micropore gas analyzer 3Flex Analyzer (Micromeritics Instruments). High pressure gas sorption studies were performed on a magnetic suspension balance marketed by Rubotherm (Germany).
